---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const repo = "https://github.com/shubham-bansal-jswone/plates-and-bars/blob/main";
---

<Base title="Licences - Plate & Bar" description="Open-source and content licences used by Plate & Bar.">
  <div class="doc"><div class="prose">
  <h1>Licences</h1>

  <h2>Our code</h2>
  <p>The source code of Plate &amp; Bar is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. See <a href={`${repo}/LICENSE`}>LICENSE</a> and <a href={`${repo}/NOTICE`}>NOTICE</a>.</p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>Content we wrote ourselves (exercise descriptions, cards, recipes and similar) is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>). You may share and adapt it if you credit Plate &amp; Bar and say if you made changes. See <a href={`${repo}/CONTENT-LICENSE`}>CONTENT-LICENSE</a>.</p>

  <h2>Fonts and icons</h2>
  <p>The site and app use Roboto and Inter, both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and the Ionicons icon font (MIT).</p>

  <h2>Third-party software</h2>
  <p>The app and site bundle open-source packages under their own licences (such as MIT, BSD and Apache 2.0). They are listed in <a href={`${repo}/THIRD_PARTY.md`}>THIRD_PARTY.md</a>.</p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
